0.1070.23 Asanother example, the CPU of the eyeglass 218 receives the identity of the seat 204A to be the seat of the sofa and assigns an alphanumeric character, such as 1b, to the identity of the seat 204A. The alphanumeric character lb assigned to the identity of the seat 204A is sometimes referred to herein as an identity Ilb.

[00115]   Figure 3B is a diagram of an embodiment of a table 350 to illustrate associations 352a, 352b, and 354. The associations 352a, 352b, and 354 are formed between a set that includes the audio data sets la, 1b, 2 and multiple audio parameters APla, APib, and AP2,and a set that includes the identities  SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1070.11 a, Ilb, and I2, the types lax, lbx, and 2x of materials of theseats 202A, 204A, 254A, 254B, and 254C and types lay, 1by, and 2y of materials of covers of the seats 202A, 204A, 254A, 254B, and 254C of the systems 200 and 250 (Figures 2A and 2B). The audio parameters APla represent the audio parameters that are determined by the feature classifier from the audio data set la. The audio data set la is generated based on the sounds received from the interaction of the user 1 with the seat 202A (Figure 2A). Also, the audio parameters APlb represent the audio parameters that are determined by the feature classifier from the audio data set lb. The audio data set lb is captured based on the sounds received from the interaction of the user 2 with the seat 204A (Figure 2A). The audio parameters AP2 represent the audio parameters that are determined by the feature classifier based on the audio data set 2. The audio data set 2 is generated based on sounds received from the interaction of the user 3 with the seat 254B (Figure 2B) or the user 6 with the seat 254A (Figure 2B) or the user 4 with the seat 254C (Figure 2B) or a combination thereof.

